WEBVTT

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:34.410
<i>Did I fight to the end?</i>

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:43.130
<i>Did I do the best I could?</i>

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.990
A Few Days Ago

00:02:22.840 --> 00:02:27.030
Sir, at least take off our handcuffs!

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:30.330
If we fall overboard like this, we're doomed!

00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:34.320
There's no need to show mercy to the exiles.

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.270
Indeed.

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:38.250
We're not gonna run away 
in the middle of the ocean!

00:02:41.490 --> 00:02:44.860
Pathetic... I was once the 
richest man in Hakozaki,

00:02:44.860 --> 00:02:48.120
and now I'm exiled along with this scum...

00:02:46.910 --> 00:02:49.540
<b>Former Retainer of the Kamakura Shogunate
Kuchii Jinzaburou</b>

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:52.490
We're gonna die!

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:53.770
No!

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:57.060
Please, sir!

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.150
We're not going to run now!

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:02.090
Very well.

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:03.740
Take off their handcuffs.

00:03:03.740 --> 00:03:04.620
Yes, sir.

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:07.350
Thank you!

00:03:07.350 --> 00:03:08.910
We'll never forget this.

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:10.410
We owe you one!

00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:12.440
I wouldn't have done that.

00:03:12.440 --> 00:03:13.770
What?

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:17.130
Do you still think you're a noble's servant?

00:03:17.650 --> 00:03:20.760
You're just a pitiful prisoner now!

00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:28.970
Let's do this, guys!

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:34.480
Don't mess with Haejirou's gang!

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:36.940
This no-name bureaucrat's going 
to the bottom of the sea!

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:44.500
There're too many people on this ship.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:49.080
Should we offer them to Wadatsumi-sama, 
the god of the sea, too?

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:56.770
This is great!

00:03:57.410 --> 00:03:58.960
Save me!

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:01.100
Please! I have money!

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:02.520
I buried it before I came here!

00:04:18.470 --> 00:04:19.820
Damn you!

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.160
Don't mess with us!

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:43.670
You, seamen! Helmsmen!

00:04:45.670 --> 00:04:47.960
If you want to survive, get to work.

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:49.850
Take us to the island!

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:54.830
Wow... What was that?

00:04:54.830 --> 00:04:57.100
He was like a demon god...

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:59.690
He ain't nothing so fancy.

00:05:00.330 --> 00:05:02.900
Hey, Kuchii Jinzaburou!

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:05.010
You look pathetic!

00:05:05.010 --> 00:05:07.610
Just two years ago, you were a proud general,

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:10.820
leading the war against the pirates!

00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:12.700
Oh, I see.

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:15.670
You're one of the pirates I captured.

00:05:12.810 --> 00:05:17.620
<b>Onitakemaru</b>

00:05:15.670 --> 00:05:17.620
I wondered why you were being so friendly.

00:05:17.620 --> 00:05:18.850
What?

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:20.340
Did you forget me?

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:23.620
I am Onitakemaru, 
the greatest pirate in the land!

00:05:23.620 --> 00:05:26.690
I can't even count how many 
pirates I've defeated.

00:05:33.350 --> 00:05:35.690
We can talk about old times later.

00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:37.970
For now, focus on getting us to the island.

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:40.790
I'll get you eventually.

00:05:44.490 --> 00:05:47.240
Hey, we're raising the mast!

00:05:47.240 --> 00:05:50.030
You're crazy! Not in this wind!

00:05:50.030 --> 00:05:55.500
When I stick something big in a hole, 
I don't stop until I'm done!

00:06:21.810 --> 00:06:23.740
We finally made it.

00:06:23.740 --> 00:06:24.730
Yeah.

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:28.360
That's Tsushima.

00:06:29.490 --> 00:06:32.090
It looks better than I expected it would.

00:06:32.090 --> 00:06:34.810
It's supposed to be the 
very far end of Japan,

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:37.000
so I wondered what I was 
getting myself into, but...

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:39.930
What is it?

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:41.530
Nothing.

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:44.170
A great shark!

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:48.130
A white shark, huh?

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:51.800
That's an umisachihiko.

00:06:52.210 --> 00:06:54.560
It's been three years since 
I've seen one myself.

00:06:54.970 --> 00:06:56.800
What a surprise.

00:06:56.800 --> 00:07:01.060
The island must be welcoming 
our newest group of exiles.

00:07:01.890 --> 00:07:03.560
How beautiful!

00:07:03.940 --> 00:07:05.820
Welcome to Tsushima!

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:09.160
I am the daughter of Sou Sukekuni, 
the ruler of this island.

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:11.030
My name is Teruhi.

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:12.970
<b>Daughter of Sou Sukekuni, The Local Ruler
Princess Teruhi</b>

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:13.570
I have come to welcome you all.

00:07:13.930 --> 00:07:16.100
You've spent two days aboard 
your boat since leaving Hakata.

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:18.020
You must be tired.

00:07:18.020 --> 00:07:22.330
We've prepared to a small 
banquet to welcome you.

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:25.040
Come this way...

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:28.260
Why even think about it?

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:31.860
We exiles have nowhere else to go.

00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:36.970
Let's do what Momotarou did, and go have a 
huge party with Otohime at Ryuuguu Palace.

00:07:40.310 --> 00:07:42.290
That was Urashima Tarou.

00:07:55.740 --> 00:07:57.450
This is great!

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:59.240
It's been two days since I've had food!

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:01.690
I'm so glad I survived!

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:04.830
They're all so tough...

00:08:04.020 --> 00:08:08.400
<b>Chouminpuku</b>

00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:07.600
I'm still barely able to stand,

00:08:07.600 --> 00:08:09.220
and my stomach feels awful...

00:08:09.220 --> 00:08:10.200
Rich man.

00:08:11.690 --> 00:08:13.510
Eat up, even if you don't want to.

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:15.320
We don't know what's coming tomorrow.

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:18.510
Exiles...

00:08:20.330 --> 00:08:22.350
Is the food to your liking?

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:24.280
Otohime-sama!

00:08:24.280 --> 00:08:26.060
Come here and pour me a drink!

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:28.980
Princess Teruhi of the Sou clan, right?

00:08:29.770 --> 00:08:31.490
Let's hear what this is about.

00:08:31.490 --> 00:08:33.440
You're Kuchii Jinzaburou-sama,

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:37.450
formerly in the service of 
the Kamakura, correct?

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:41.970
What do you mean by that, exactly?

00:08:41.970 --> 00:08:43.880
There's no way you didn't 
notice that there was nobody

00:08:43.880 --> 00:08:45.400
from the government aboard that ship.

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:47.080
And yet we're being warmly welcomed.

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:49.590
There must be some reason.

00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:53.090
Not at all, Kuchii-sama.

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:57.050
We simply wish that all of you will fight with

00:08:57.050 --> 00:09:00.930
all your strength for 
the sake of this island.

00:09:01.880 --> 00:09:03.150
Fight?

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:04.890
Fight what?

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:07.440
The Mukuri.

00:09:09.590 --> 00:09:11.900
Mukuri? The Mongolians?

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:15.980
You must have heard the rumors, I'm sure,

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:20.410
about a vast army of Mukuri invading 
the land of the rising sun.

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:23.660
They are almost upon us.

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:29.060
I am told the Gappo inlet in Goryeo 
is covered with thousands of warships.

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:29.670
Goryeo Gappo

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:35.170
Their first target will be Tsushima.

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:41.310
So you asked the Kamakura to exile anybody 
who could help in a war to this place?

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:44.290
We submitted an official request 
through the Dazaifu magistrate,

00:09:44.290 --> 00:09:45.980
which they could not refuse.

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:50.930
You were all to be put to death to begin with.

00:09:50.930 --> 00:09:52.230
In other words...

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:55.110
We saved your lives.

00:10:03.570 --> 00:10:05.450
I thought it was something like this.

00:10:05.970 --> 00:10:07.130
Hell no!

00:10:07.130 --> 00:10:09.630
This is no different than being put to death!

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:13.250
You bitch! I'll make you pay for—

00:10:19.220 --> 00:10:21.640
Now, all of you...

00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:26.360
Die for the sake of Tsushima.

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:32.950
The alcohol wore off.

00:10:32.950 --> 00:10:34.490
Fight the Mongolians?

00:10:34.490 --> 00:10:35.610
That's insane.

00:10:35.610 --> 00:10:38.320
Are they really going to attack?

00:10:38.320 --> 00:10:40.200
Not after all this time.

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:43.380
I heard a rumor an ambassador of theirs 
came to us about three years ago,

00:10:43.380 --> 00:10:44.820
and then nothing.

00:10:44.820 --> 00:10:47.810
Kuchii-dono, what will you do?

00:10:47.810 --> 00:10:50.290
Will you join the island's army and fight?

00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:52.390
I don't know.

00:10:53.910 --> 00:10:56.630
But I figured something had to be up.

00:10:57.250 --> 00:11:00.340
I wouldn't normally get off 
with just exile for what I did.

00:11:00.980 --> 00:11:02.290
It's the same for you all, right?

00:11:24.010 --> 00:11:26.660
You did well to endure all that, Princess.

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:30.150
Otaki.

00:11:30.150 --> 00:11:32.120
I don't like murder.

00:11:32.650 --> 00:11:35.910
No, this is only the beginning, I'm sure.

00:11:35.910 --> 00:11:38.410
Once the war starts, even more will...

00:11:39.610 --> 00:11:41.630
The bath is ready.

00:11:41.630 --> 00:11:44.490
Warm yourself and calm down.

00:11:57.010 --> 00:12:01.100
By the way, where is this Tsushima place?

00:12:01.100 --> 00:12:02.930
You know, monk?

00:12:02.930 --> 00:12:03.950
No.

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:06.130
I don't know much about faraway lands.

00:12:06.130 --> 00:12:07.300
You?

00:12:07.300 --> 00:12:09.870
It's my first time outside 
the land I was born in.

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:13.890
Hey, you old geezer. Do you know?

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:16.290
Who do you think you're talking to, brat?

00:12:16.770 --> 00:12:20.810
I'm a merchant, unlike you country hicks!

00:12:20.810 --> 00:12:22.470
I owned a map of Japan.

00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:26.290
The island of Tsushima is on the right side,

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:31.980
<b>Hakata</b>

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:31.980
<b>Iki</b>

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:31.980
<b>Tsushima</b>

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:31.980
<b>Goryeo</b>

00:12:26.710 --> 00:12:28.820
that is, the west side,

00:12:28.820 --> 00:12:31.270
in between Goryeo and Kyuushuu.

00:12:31.940 --> 00:12:35.310
So when merchant ships travel 
between Goryeo and Hakata,

00:12:35.310 --> 00:12:37.400
they first pass through Tsushima.

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:43.680
I never imagined I'd be here 
under such circumstances, though.

00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:48.100
It's all the fault of those eastern 
barbarians in the Kamakura.

00:12:48.100 --> 00:12:50.660
The way they run their government...

00:12:51.730 --> 00:12:52.790
Right, right.

00:12:53.810 --> 00:12:56.590
If the Mongolian Navy is truly on its way,

00:12:56.590 --> 00:12:59.080
it's true that this island 
will be their first stop.

00:12:59.510 --> 00:13:00.670
But that doesn't make

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:05.510
the idea of dying in a place you've 
got nothing to do with any less scary.

00:13:06.170 --> 00:13:11.520
<i>So now I'm a prisoner, sent all the way 
to the end of Japan to fight a war...</i>

00:13:12.580 --> 00:13:16.740
<i>No matter where I go, it's another war...</i>

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:41.940
<i>What will happen to Tsushima?</i>

00:13:43.050 --> 00:13:44.870
<i>Will the Mukuri take it?</i>

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:47.630
<i>The land, the people?</i>

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:52.390
<i>No, maybe the Mukuri will never come.</i>

00:13:53.290 --> 00:13:56.410
<i>Maybe we're doing this for nothing...</i>

00:13:57.890 --> 00:14:00.150
Otaki, you get some rest, as well.

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:01.400
Very well.

00:14:06.550 --> 00:14:08.740
<i>I'm no good...</i>

00:14:09.240 --> 00:14:10.950
<i>I ran again.</i>

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:14.640
<i>If someone throws a stone at 
you, you can close your eyes,</i>

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:16.390
<i>but it will still hit you...</i>

00:14:19.990 --> 00:14:21.330
Princess!

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:23.710
Princess, run—

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:24.920
Otaki?!

00:14:31.190 --> 00:14:32.610
Princess!

00:14:32.610 --> 00:14:33.310
Run—

00:14:47.610 --> 00:14:49.170
Intruders!

00:14:49.170 --> 00:14:50.610
The princess!

00:14:50.610 --> 00:14:51.340
Hurry!

00:14:51.340 --> 00:14:54.120
Hilarious. The guards left.

00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:56.280
They're so disorganized...

00:14:56.280 --> 00:14:58.290
But it's perfect for us.

00:15:00.410 --> 00:15:02.470
Somebody's trying to get 
into the princess's bed?

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:05.270
The noise is coming from over there.

00:15:05.270 --> 00:15:07.860
The soldiers are just 
running around helpless.

00:15:07.860 --> 00:15:08.890
You can see them?

00:15:08.890 --> 00:15:10.020
Yeah.

00:15:10.020 --> 00:15:11.380
I can see at night.

00:15:13.410 --> 00:15:16.010
Well, either way, it's good news for us.

00:15:16.010 --> 00:15:17.700
Heaven has favored us.

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:19.650
The Buddha is on our side.

00:15:19.650 --> 00:15:23.900
Let's raid the fisherman's homes and have 
them send us back to Hakata by boat!

00:15:23.900 --> 00:15:27.750
Wait, you're going to try and cross 
those awful seas in a fisherman's boat?

00:15:27.750 --> 00:15:31.180
They say that one out of three of the 
bigger ships don't survive the trip.

00:15:31.180 --> 00:15:33.640
You might be better off 
fighting the Mongolians.

00:15:33.640 --> 00:15:37.110
You just want to fight a war, don't you?

00:15:37.110 --> 00:15:38.370
Don't be stupid.

00:15:38.370 --> 00:15:39.500
What would be in it for me?

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:41.150
I don't know...

00:15:41.150 --> 00:15:44.040
You look like a dog that's found its prey.

00:15:45.220 --> 00:15:46.800
So do you.

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:49.490
The three of us will be splitting up.

00:15:49.490 --> 00:15:51.570
We're bandits and mountain monks.

00:15:51.570 --> 00:15:53.530
We can hide in the mountains 
if we can't take a boat.

00:15:53.530 --> 00:15:54.620
Well, you guys...

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:55.760
Farewell.

00:15:55.760 --> 00:15:56.550
Yeah.

00:15:57.540 --> 00:16:01.060
Now, I'm going to kill some time...

00:16:01.960 --> 00:16:05.690
by burning this whole place to the ground.

00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:08.260
Look carefully!

00:16:08.260 --> 00:16:11.190
The intruders are somewhere in this darkness.

00:16:11.190 --> 00:16:12.610
Find them!

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:14.560
I have shamed myself!

00:16:12.610 --> 00:16:16.430
<b>Princess Teruhi's Servant
Kaitani Gontarou</b>

00:16:14.560 --> 00:16:17.910
Our lord entrusted me with the princess, but...

00:16:19.990 --> 00:16:22.310
The exiles? Curse them!

00:16:22.310 --> 00:16:24.480
Rebelling now, of all times!

00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:26.670
Gontarou-dono, look!

00:16:27.830 --> 00:16:28.900
That's her!

00:16:28.900 --> 00:16:30.260
Over there!

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:32.010
The fire helped us!

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:35.220
Princess, I'm coming!

00:16:35.410 --> 00:16:36.840
We're heading to the beach, fast.

00:16:36.840 --> 00:16:39.890
Get close to the hostage. 
They can't shoot at her.

00:16:40.310 --> 00:16:41.890
<i>A foreign language...</i>

00:16:42.280 --> 00:16:43.860
There are only six of them!

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:45.210
Don't use your bows!

00:16:45.210 --> 00:16:48.310
Get around them and surround them!

00:16:52.790 --> 00:16:53.780
They're skilled warriors?!

00:16:54.770 --> 00:16:56.760
Pathetic.

00:17:07.930 --> 00:17:09.570
Not bad, I guess.

00:17:26.390 --> 00:17:28.130
So that's the warrior from the east?

00:17:29.320 --> 00:17:31.530
He uses the Gikei style.

00:17:31.530 --> 00:17:32.410
Gikei?

00:17:32.410 --> 00:17:34.440
I've heard rumors of it.

00:17:34.830 --> 00:17:37.350
Gikei is the style used by Yoshitsune.

00:17:38.070 --> 00:17:40.310
A style of fighting created 
by the great general

00:17:40.310 --> 00:17:43.450
of the Genji a century ago, 
Genkurou Yoshitsune.

00:17:45.530 --> 00:17:47.420
Genkurou Yoshitsune?

00:17:58.500 --> 00:18:00.050
<i>This one's...</i>

00:18:34.020 --> 00:18:36.130
So you use the Gikei style, as well?

00:18:58.900 --> 00:19:00.150
Foreign ships?

00:19:04.470 --> 00:19:05.810
Who was that?

00:19:08.450 --> 00:19:11.710
In the end, you wound up getting involved.

00:19:12.450 --> 00:19:15.960
Well, it doesn't matter to me, 
as long as it's fun.

00:19:17.080 --> 00:19:18.420
I'm not like you.

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:42.980
Otaki, I'm sorry.

00:19:43.640 --> 00:19:45.410
You must have suffered so much...

00:19:48.410 --> 00:19:51.490
All of these people were born 
and raised on this island.

00:19:51.490 --> 00:19:53.720
I've known them all since I was a child.

00:19:58.180 --> 00:19:59.630
Gontarou?

00:20:00.150 --> 00:20:02.630
Give them a proper burial.

00:20:03.810 --> 00:20:06.140
War is a sad thing.

00:20:06.140 --> 00:20:07.670
War?

00:20:07.670 --> 00:20:09.930
Fool, this was just a little scrap.

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:12.190
War is a whole different beast.

00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:18.040
It takes more people, more resources, 
and a stronger mind.

00:20:19.370 --> 00:20:21.160
You don't know a damn thing,

00:20:21.160 --> 00:20:23.990
so I don't know where you get off 
telling others to fight for you.

00:20:25.210 --> 00:20:30.160
But everyone here did the best 
they could before they died.

00:20:30.160 --> 00:20:32.040
I won't say they're happy about it,

00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:36.540
but I'm sure they have no regrets.

00:20:37.480 --> 00:20:41.510
Do you have the stomach to be the 
person they'd want you to be?

00:20:46.600 --> 00:20:47.750
I have a duty...

00:20:49.290 --> 00:20:52.810
to protect this island and the people on it.

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:57.440
I won't lose anyone else!

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:03.220
And you're going to work hard 
to help me, Kuchii Jinzaburou!

00:21:04.980 --> 00:21:06.770
You did well last night.

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:08.840
I shall give you a reward later.

00:21:13.880 --> 00:21:15.110
That's great.

00:21:15.110 --> 00:21:20.310
The famous Kuchii Jinzaburou-sama, 
receiving a reward from a little girl.

00:21:20.310 --> 00:21:22.670
I'm not famous at all.

00:21:23.160 --> 00:21:24.760
Princess!

00:21:25.880 --> 00:21:26.770
Kano?

00:21:26.770 --> 00:21:28.800
You're supposed to be at the capital!

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:29.510
<b>Princess Teruhi's Servant
Kano</b>

00:21:28.800 --> 00:21:29.510
They're coming!

00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:35.020
A message from from 
the ones watching Goryeo.

00:21:36.740 --> 00:21:40.690
Warships are leaving Gappo 
port one after another.

00:21:41.220 --> 00:21:43.030
The Mongolians are coming!

00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:48.530
<i>October 3rd. The 11th year of the Bun'ei era.</i>

00:21:50.450 --> 00:21:55.960
<i>900 Mongolian warships that 
had been filling Gappo bay in Goryeo</i>

00:21:56.820 --> 00:21:58.930
<i>all weighed anchor at once...</i>

00:22:01.490 --> 00:22:06.970
<i>The eastern expedition of the 
Mongolian Empire had begun.</i>

00:22:06.970 --> 00:22:09.970
<b>Episode 1:
The Far End of Japan</b>
